## About the standard

ISO/IEC 27001 is the international standard for establishing, implementing, maintaining and continually improving an information security management system (ISMS). The 2022 version covers the updated controls in ISO/IEC 27002.

## What the standard requires

- Establish an information security management system
- Identify and manage information security risks
- Apply controls from Annex A based on a statement of applicability
- Audit and continually improve the system

## Certification

Organisations can be certified against the standard by accredited certification bodies. Certification is voluntary but is often used to demonstrate that requirements in e.g. NIS2 are handled systematically.

